<%- include('layout-start.ejs', { title: 'Configuration — Panels DCC', basePath, activeNav: 'getting-started' }) %>
<div class="main-container">
    <div class="getting-started-layout">
        <%- include('sidebar-docs.ejs', { basePath, manualChapter: 2 }) %>
        <div class="getting-started-layout-main">
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h1>Chapter 2 — Configuration</h1>
                    <p>Configuration happens on the <strong>Panels DCC website</strong> in a browser — on your sofa, at a desk, or anywhere you have internet. You do not need to be next to the layout. When you are ready to run trains, <strong>PanelsDCC Control</strong> on the Raspberry Pi uses what you have set up here.</p>
                    <p>Everything is visual. There is no requirement to write scripts or edit configuration files. If you can click, type, and drag, you can add locomotives, accessories, and control panels.</p>
                    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= panelsAppOrigin %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Panels DCC website</a></p>
                    <p>Complete <strong><a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/installation.html">Getting started</a></strong> first (install, Wi‑Fi, Connect, <a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/first-train.html">first train</a>, and <a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/account.html">your account</a>) so Control can talk to your command station.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>Recommended order</h2>
                    <ol>
                        <li><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/trains.html">Trains</a> — add locomotives and their DCC numbers.</li>
                        <li><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/function-maps.html">Functions and function maps</a> — icons for lights, horns, and other decoder features (optional until you want more than a basic throttle).</li>
                        <li><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/accessories.html">Accessories</a> — points, signals, and other layout items.</li>
                        <li><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/panels.html">Panels</a> — draw the diagram you will operate from, and link it to those accessories.</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p>Sensors, train detection, and route setting will be covered in later chapters. This chapter is the everyday setup path.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>1. Trains</h2>
                    <p>Your cloud library of locomotives, coaches, and wagons: pictures, status, DCC address, decoder notes, and function icons. Quick-add from the UK library, or enter details by hand.</p>
                    <p><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/trains.html">Open Configuration — Trains</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>2. Accessories</h2>
                    <p>Create points, colour-light and semaphore signals, crossings, and custom items. Each state has a DCC number. Macros group several accessories so you can set them together later in Control.</p>
                    <p><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/accessories.html">Open Configuration — Accessories</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>3. Panels</h2>
                    <p>A panel is a control diagram of your layout — not a scale track plan. Place track, points, and signals, then link them to the accessories you have already created (or create a missing accessory without leaving the editor).</p>
                    <p><a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/panels.html">Open Configuration — Panels</a></p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <%- include('getting-started-pager.ejs', {
                pagerPrevHref: basePath + '/getting-started/account.html',
                pagerPrevTitle: 'Your PanelsDCC account',
                pagerNextHref: basePath + '/configuration/trains.html',
                pagerNextTitle: 'Trains'
            }) %>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<%- include('layout-end.ejs') %>
